From dupan at northwestern.edu  Tue Jun  3 23:22:53 2008
From: dupan at northwestern.edu (Pan Du)
Date: Tue, 03 Jun 2008 16:22:53 -0500
Subject: [BioC] lumi annotation package
In-Reply-To: <B4A5EC31F6F6A9498CBD960808F9F3B80FD27F@mailbox12.cshl.edu>
Message-ID: <C46B205D.69CA%dupan@northwestern.edu>

Hi Xiaoyue,

The lumiHumanAll.db package includes all the Illumina Human expression
chips. You can use it for annotation purpose of HumanWG-6_V3 chip. However,
unlike lumiHumanV1 or lumiHumanV2, it does not include the mapping
information between the Illumina ID and nuID. In the near future, we plan to
create a separate package for Illumina id mapping purpose.

If your BeadStudio output file includes the probe sequence information,
lumiR can automatically covert the data as nuID annotated, then you can use
lumiHumanAll.db package without any problem.


Pan


