From naomi at stat.psu.edu  Wed Jun  4 22:50:07 2008
From: naomi at stat.psu.edu (Naomi Altman)
Date: Wed, 04 Jun 2008 16:50:07 -0400
Subject: [BioC] Limma design question (model interactions)
In-Reply-To: <4846E89B.40900@igbmc.u-strasbg.fr>
References: <4846E89B.40900@igbmc.u-strasbg.fr>
Message-ID: <6.2.3.4.2.20080604164703.02689fd0@imap.stat.psu.edu>

You have a compound hypothesis, so you will need to do 2 contrasts:

i.e. you want B=Ref intersect A != Ref

Interaction means that the effect of B depends on 
the level of A observed.  Since you do not 
observe A and B together in the same samples, you cannot test interaction.

--Naomi


