Dear Steve
I suggest you to download the latest version of oneChannelGUI 1.6.2
Due to various problems with cdfs I moved, in the latest version of oneChannelGUI, to the use of APT tools for the calculation of probe set summaries also for gene arrays.

You have to install by yourself APT tools on your computer. Than using the function "oneChannelGUI: Set Affymetrix apt tools folder" located in the general menu you will set the apt tool parameter in oneChannelGUI. Subsequently with the function "oneChannelGUI: Set library folder and install Affy gene/Exon library files" you will install in the oneChannelGUI dir all the Affymetrix library files needed to analyze gene and exon arrays.

There is in "file" menu a specific radio button for GENE arrays. 
Ones summaries are calculated those are stored in an ExpressionSet object and you can analyze them using any of the statistical tools interfaced in oneChannelGUI.

