I had a stats professor tell me that theoretically you are performing a
test each time you filter a gene (based on fold change or standard
deviation, etc.). So if you go along with that line of thinking, you
wouldn't really be helping with the multiple testing problem and may be
artificially lowering your p-values.

I am new to this area of research, though, so I don't know what the
standard practices are for publishing this type of result.

-Steve

